The authorized adapter correction is complete, and the integrity audit confirms it is the only source change.

The unknown-user failure comes from this fallback in `hw6UserNodeIndex()` (`script.js:1563–1564`). After all raw-ID lookups fail, it treats the raw ID as a node index. The proposed correction is:

```diff
-  const numeric = Number(userId);
-  return Number.isFinite(numeric) && numeric >= 0 && numeric < hw6NodeCount(graph) ? numeric : -1;
+  return -1;
```

This would let the existing caller reject unknown users while preserving valid mapped users. It has not been applied.

